+++ b/docs/change_log/release-3.4.md
@@ -58,6 +58,21 @@ In addition, the `md_globals` parameter of
 `Markdown.extensions.Extension.extendMarkdown()` is no longer recognized as a
 valid parameter and will raise an error if provided.
 
+### The `UnescapePostprocessor` has been deprecated
+
+The `markdown.postprocessors.UnescapePostprocessor` has been deprecated in favor
+of the new `markdown.treeprocessors.UnescapeTreeprocessor`, which is registered
+by default under the name `unescape` with a priority of `0`. Backslash-escaped
+characters are now restored in the ElementTree before it is serialized, so that
+the serializer properly escapes them. Previously, an escaped character such as
+`\"` (when the [smarty] extension is enabled) could produce invalid HTML when
+used in an attribute value (i.e. `![x\"x](x)` resulted in `alt="x"x"`).
+As a side effect, escaped characters such as `\>` are now output as entities
+(`&gt;`) where appropriate. Extensions which deregister or depend upon the
+`unescape` postprocessor should be updated accordingly.
+
+[smarty]: ../extensions/smarty.md
+
 ## New features
 
 The following new features have been included in the 3.4 release:
@@ -97,3 +112,6 @@ The following bug fixes are included in the 3.4 release:
 
 * Extension entry-points are only loaded if needed (#1216).
 * Added additional checks to the `<pre><code>` handling of `PrettifyTreeprocessor` (#1261, #1263).
+* Backslash-escaped characters are now properly escaped by the serializer when
+  used in attribute values, which previously could result in invalid HTML when
+  using the `smarty` extension.
